{"id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000f4:0","agent":"claude-code","sessionId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ad","projectPath":"C:\\Users\\dev\\Downloads\\billion-context-0.1.208\\billion-context-0.1.208","ts":"2026-10-27T17:03:21.520Z","seq":26,"kind":"reply","text":"The CLI is installed, but I stopped before the \"apply to all future sessions\" step. What it gives Claude Code isn't a set of skills, so I'd rather check with you first.\n\n**Version:** I installed 0.1.208. The registry's `latest` tag points to it, and the many other versions there are automatic per-PR builds, so this is the stable release. `bili --version` reports `0.1.208 (b261c333)`.\n\n**What the Claude Code integration does:** it's one command, `bili plugin install claude` (the `/bili-setup` file in the package just runs it). According to the README, it:\n- **Routes all your Claude Code traffic through a local proxy.** It sets `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` in your user settings, so every request, including your auth, goes through this third-party program running on your machine. The proxy compresses conversation history so very long sessions can keep going.\n- **Turns off Claude Code's built-in auto-compaction** (`DISABLE_AUTO_COMPACT=1`) so the proxy handles compression instead.\n- **Adds a start…","meta":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
