{"id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000100:0","agent":"claude-code","sessionId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ad","projectPath":"C:\\Users\\dev\\Downloads\\billion-context-0.1.208\\billion-context-0.1.208","ts":"2026-10-27T17:05:56.448Z","seq":30,"kind":"reply","text":"Yes. Use the launcher, `bili claude`, instead of the plugin install, and desktop sessions won't be touched at all.\n\nI checked the README for how the launcher works:\n- **It doesn't edit any config files.** `bili claude` starts its own proxy and points only the Claude Code session it launches at that proxy, through environment variables set for that one process. Your settings file stays as it is.\n- **Desktop sessions keep working normally.** The Code tab never reads those variables, so it runs directly with Claude Code's built-in auto-compaction, exactly as it does now.\n- **No compaction conflict.** Inside a `bili claude` session, the launcher lines up Claude Code's own auto-compact threshold with bili's compression limit, so the two don't fight.\n\nSo the setup would be:\n- **Terminal, with bili:** run `bili claude` instead of `claude`.\n- **Terminal, without bili:** plain `claude`, unchanged.\n- **Desktop app:** unchanged.\n\nIf you want bili on by default in the terminal, I can add a small f…","meta":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
